WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.500
 

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.000
 

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.000
 

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:25.235
Hey everybody it's Charlie. time to start the conversation

00:00:25.235 --> 00:00:28.000
about season 8 so we could do this for like an hour

00:00:28.055 --> 00:00:30.855
long so this is going to be top 10 then we can pick bonus

00:00:30.855 --> 00:00:33.775
videos for other really important stuff like all the

00:00:33.775 --> 00:00:39.645
Aegon backstory why Jon is named Aegon instead Jaeharys their will be a lot of stuff to get through and I

00:00:39.645 --> 00:00:42.485
will still be doing the Game of Thrones giveaway week to week

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:45.485
during the off season how ever long it takes to season 8

00:00:45.485 --> 00:00:48.460
but lets actually start with that so number 10 their starting

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:51.240
to shoot season 8 like actually film episodes with

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:54.240
the actors in October. That doesn't 100%

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:57.240
confirm that they are going to finish everything by next year and

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:00.100
get it out by the summer but its a strong possibility

00:01:00.105 --> 00:01:02.545
There was a big question earlier this year about

00:01:02.545 --> 00:01:05.005
how long it was going to take them to write the scripts. There's only

00:01:05.005 --> 00:01:08.065
six episodes. It sound like they'll all be longer than an hour

00:01:08.065 --> 00:01:11.055
maybe not quite as long as this finale

00:01:11.055 --> 00:01:13.205
but maybe close to it. Feature

00:01:13.205 --> 00:01:16.200
length is usually something you'd use to describe something that's longer than

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:19.120
an hour. So I'm expecting all the episodes to be

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:21.645
at least longer than an hour but like episode 4

00:01:21.645 --> 00:01:24.625
this season was one of the best episodes of the season was shorter

00:01:24.625 --> 00:01:27.335
than 50 minutes so episode length isn't necessarily

00:01:27.335 --> 00:01:30.405
an indicator of episode quality. But starting

00:01:30.405 --> 00:01:33.435
with actually Night King stuff, starting from the end of the episode,

00:01:33.435 --> 00:01:35.965
so he makes it south of the Wall. Really what

00:01:35.965 --> 00:01:38.905
he's probably going to do is just patrol the North and grab

00:01:38.905 --> 00:01:41.365
everybody that he can. What's the

00:01:41.365 --> 00:01:44.285
first big thing here south of the Wall? The Last Hearth

00:01:44.285 --> 00:01:47.325
so he's probably gonna sweep over most of these minor

00:01:47.325 --> 00:01:50.175
houses like Deepwood Motte, the Karhold

00:01:50.175 --> 00:01:52.905
but I think the deeper meaning is you get a form of a redemption

00:01:52.905 --> 00:01:55.935
for these former traitor houses like you have Alice

00:01:55.935 --> 00:01:59.105
Karstark. She and all her people, the Umbers, they might wind up

00:01:59.105 --> 00:02:01.695
dying but the Night King is basically just gonna snake

00:02:01.695 --> 00:02:04.135
his way south as he gets to Winterfell

00:02:04.135 --> 00:02:07.185
Obviously Winterfell is going to be one of the big huge

00:02:07.185 --> 00:02:10.125
battles of the season, probably early on by

00:02:10.125 --> 00:02:12.985
the middle of the season at least, it depends on how time passes

00:02:12.985 --> 00:02:16.035
between episodes. But for those of you asking about Thormund

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:18.685
and Beric, yes, I believe they made it down the

00:02:18.685 --> 00:02:21.365
Wall they just didn't show you them escaping but if

00:02:21.365 --> 00:02:24.405
you haven't seen the body that means that they are probably still alive

00:02:24.405 --> 00:02:27.275
so don't worry about them. They either made it into the bay

00:02:27.275 --> 00:02:30.295
and they are sailing south or they made it to the Last

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:33.275
Hearth and that's where they'll pop up next, like Thormund's

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:36.365
too amazing to get rid of in an off-screen moment, so I think that all the

00:02:36.365 --> 00:02:39.415
people that died in the Wall coming down are just Red Shirts.

00:02:39.415 --> 00:02:42.465
But #9 in service of really great moments

00:02:42.465 --> 00:02:45.375
With Tyrion and Cersei, the episode

00:02:45.375 --> 00:02:48.295
 

00:02:48.295 --> 00:02:51.315
 

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:54.300
So we will be able to have an equal balance of both,

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:56.880
but i still think they will try to do at least one big hard-home

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:59.400
style episode, where you are just consumed with the

00:02:59.405 --> 00:03:02.205
single plot line, get a really big action-set piece

00:03:02.205 --> 00:03:05.205
that also sort of weaves in a little bit of character stuff.

00:03:05.205 --> 00:03:07.675
Hard-home is still one of the best, if not the best

00:03:07.675 --> 00:03:10.775
big action set piece of the TV show has ever done,

00:03:10.775 --> 00:03:12.495
if not best episode out-right.

00:03:12.495 --> 00:03:18.345
So I'm gonna cross my finger that they are able to get some of their A list directors, because there were couple of directors

00:03:18.345 --> 00:03:21.025
they were not able to bring back this season for scheduling reasons.

00:03:21.025 --> 00:03:24.075
So hopefully they can bring back the best of the best

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:27.240
when it comes to making the episodes. But a lot

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:33.125
of those really awesome character moments were just predicated on the odd pairings of people that you don't normally see together

00:03:33.125 --> 00:03:36.075
like the hound and brienne, so i am hoping for more of that.

00:03:36.075 --> 00:03:39.015
Bran can go anywhere with his mind, and Samwell is a character

00:03:39.015 --> 00:03:41.805
that just brings so much comedy with him. But he has

00:03:41.805 --> 00:03:44.775
all this knowledge from citadel too.

